uired row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a209cc4-1bab-5ab0-9215-a0c12fc7abc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638672} {:answer/id #uuid "463567ff-d1fb-5fae-a423-d6c87f60ea9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638753} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ecab8a-4cc6-5ec6-b06f-ce1f799d9536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638953} {:answer/id #uuid "dcab087d-6d59-55b7-926d-bee265aa38a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639013} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd4b0eb-a3f2-550a-a0ae-d511778ff783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a209cc4-1bab-5ab0-9215-a0c12fc7abc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638672} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4ffec46-b84a-54ac-9282-39650928171d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639156}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "372c1499-bf5a-558e-ad8a-af28e6ae7898" :question/math-academy-id "q-72858" :question/problem "Given that\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{23}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bm