_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db4e6b7-6a4d-5faf-abb2-9e45c22c8391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671630} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75dd3b3-878d-507c-83d2-a5d4d221fd77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671652}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b461d4d8-7459-5734-9051-0ff4e01dc9bd" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{21}=0$?" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{21}=9+(-3)\\cdot (3)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D &=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -21 & -11 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{3}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}]}
